.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-ADD-OBJECT-ATTRIBUTE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-add-object-attribute \- add an attribute to a storage object
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm add-object-attribute
.BR \-\-ern | \-e
.I ERN
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
.BR \-\-value | \-v
.I VALUE
[\fB\-\-type\fR|\fB\-t\fR \fITYPE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds a user-defined attribute to a storage object. Attributes are
metadata the object's owner attaches to it; the storage module never
interprets them, unlike the content type or checksum it derives from
the object's bytes itself.
.PP
The object must not carry an attribute of that name yet - this action
refuses to overwrite one, so a mistyped name is reported instead of
quietly creating a second attribute. Use
.BR euclid-cli-esm-set-object-attribute (1)
to change a value that already exists.
.PP
A value keeps its type across storage and retrieval, so a number
stored as a number is read back as one. Prints the stored attribute as
JSON on success.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the object. Required.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Attribute name. Required.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-value " " \fIVALUE\fR
Attribute value, as text; interpreted according to
.BR \-\-type .
Required.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Type of the value: one of \fIint\fR, \fIlong\fR, \fIdouble\fR,
\fIfloat\fR, \fIbool\fR, \fIstring\fR or \fIbinary\fR. Defaults to
\fIstring\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The attribute was added. The stored attribute is printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, no object
with that ERN exists, the object belongs to another account, or the
object already has an attribute of that name.
.SH EXAMPLES
Tag an object with the pipeline that produced it:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm add-object-attribute \e
    --ern ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:development:object:mix/PIM-4269.xml \e
    --name source --value pim
.fi
.RE
.PP
Record a revision number as a number rather than as text:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm add-object-attribute \e
    --ern ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:development:object:mix/PIM-4269.xml \e
    --name revision --value 7 --type long
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-set-object-attribute (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-object-attributes (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-object-attribute (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-objects (1)
